abstract: >
  SIRIUS LOCAL AI is a fully modular, offline-only AI runtime designed for secure,
  deterministic execution of commands, workflows, plugins, reasoning tasks, and
  semantic automation. Version 5.9.1 introduces a major architectural leap with a
  native dual-language Knowledge Graph architecture (autosave_kg.json for SK and
  autosave_kg_en.json for EN) that completely segregates linguistic knowledge stores
  and eliminates cross-lingual contamination. It integrates a native lossless entity
  merge engine (kg merge) inside RuntimeCore, enables context-aware taxonomical
  inference (KG_VERIFY) recognizing biological sub-taxa with persistent edge auto-commits,
  and delivers robust reverse location querying with anti-flora classification guards.

  Version 5.9.1 further hardens system safety and stability through greedy trailing
  punctuation stripping (.rstrip("?")), confirmation state latching across interactive
  turns, a hard Token Guard against malicious character sequences, an automated 100-file
  sliding-window quarantine rotator, TerminalAssistant with 0.0s blocking of forbidden
  commands, and a Human-in-the-Loop Safe Trash pipeline that prevents direct file destruction.
  Execution is driven centrally by sirius_orchestrator.py through an integrated single-process
  IPC Daemon running natively on port 8080.

  The system operates entirely on the user's device without cloud dependencies or
  external data transmission. All operations adhere to strict security boundaries,
  customs validation through COLNIK-6.x, autonomous supervision via AUTONOMY-6.x,
  TimeCore latency profiling, Guard monitoring, and auditable symbolic explainability.
